Chapter: BvtGuardFall
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeFighter
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtLeash
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-143 (trial 43060: owner row 26, serial 2152, a Britain guard that bought a gorget, cg-guard-buy): an NPC whose owner
 row no settler names loses it at the blow. Answers a bit per check: 1 both rows are held before, 2 the guard's row is gone
 after cg-deaths, 4 the bystander's row stays and the count drops by one; 7 is all, negative when not buildable.
  bgf-mobile : CompositeGame -> Integer
  bgf-mobile (owner) = when world-create owner.checkpoint.game.world (gs-mobile 0 1450 1600 0 400 1002) is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (serial) -> serial
  bgf-checks : Integer -> Integer
  bgf-checks (unused) = when blh-owner 0
    is Err (_) -> -1
    is Ok (owner) -> when owner.spawns
      is None -> -2
      is Just (g) -> let v = owner.vendor
        in let guard = bgf-mobile owner
        in let other = bgf-mobile owner
        in let ga = cg-crew-actor owner 77001
        in let oa = cg-crew-actor owner 77002
        in if guard == 0 | other == 0 | ga < 1 | oa < 1 then -3
        else let r1 = cgf-register v guard ga 0
        in let r2 = cgf-register v other oa 0
        in let rows = v.owner-count
        in let held = gv-owner v guard 0 >= 0 & gv-owner v other 0 >= 0
        in let died = cg-deaths owner g 0 guard
        in (if held then 1 else 0) + (if gv-owner v guard 0 < 0 then 2 else 0) + (if gv-owner v other 0 >= 0 & v.owner-count == rows - 1 then 4 else 0)
  bvt-guard-fall : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-guard-fall (unused) = act
    n <- bgf-checks 0
    bvt-check ("a guard or any NPC holding an owner row loses the row when it dies, and no other row moves (UOAIX-143, code " & show n & ")") (n == 7)
  end
